IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpfta-types`
IMPORT `cpfta-part3a-investigation`

-- Tests for Part 3A (ss 19 to 26).  Thresholds read off the text: at least 2 working
-- days' notice (s 21(2)(a)); a warrant "continues in force for one month beginning on the
-- day on which the warrant is issued" (s 22(6)).

§ `Tests -- Part 3A`

§§ `19. Power to investigate`

--                                             supplier suspected, past abetting, present abetting
`a supplier suspected of an unfair practice` MEANS `Suspicion Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a person suspected of having abetted` MEANS `Suspicion Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`a person suspected of abetting now` MEANS `Suspicion Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`no suspicion` MEANS `Suspicion Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the Commission may conduct an investigation` `a supplier suspected of an unfair practice`
#ASSERT `the Commission may conduct an investigation` `a person suspected of having abetted`
#ASSERT `the Commission may conduct an investigation` `a person suspected of abetting now`
#ASSERT NOT `the Commission may conduct an investigation` `no suspicion`

-- Officer Facts: chief executive appointed, kind of appointee, declared office, produced the card on demand, refuses.
`a Commission employee appointed by the chief executive who declared office and showed the card` MEANS `Officer Facts` OF TRUE, `an officer or employee of the Commission`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a Commission employee who did not declare office` MEANS `Officer Facts` OF TRUE, `an officer or employee of the Commission`, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`an auxiliary police officer who did not declare office` MEANS `Officer Facts` OF TRUE, `an auxiliary police officer appointed under Part 9 of the Police Force Act 2004`, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`an auxiliary police officer who refused to show the card` MEANS `Officer Facts` OF TRUE, `an auxiliary police officer appointed under Part 9 of the Police Force Act 2004`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a stranger appointed by the chief executive` MEANS `Officer Facts` OF TRUE, `any other person`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`an employee appointed by someone other than the chief executive` MEANS `Officer Facts` OF FALSE, `an officer or employee of the Commission`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the person is validly appointed an investigation officer` `a Commission employee appointed by the chief executive who declared office and showed the card`
#ASSERT `the person is validly appointed an investigation officer` `an auxiliary police officer who did not declare office`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is validly appointed an investigation officer` `a stranger appointed by the chief executive`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is validly appointed an investigation officer` `an employee appointed by someone other than the chief executive`
#ASSERT `the officer has complied with section 19(3)` `a Commission employee appointed by the chief executive who declared office and showed the card`
#ASSERT NOT `the officer has complied with section 19(3)` `a Commission employee who did not declare office`
#ASSERT `the officer has complied with section 19(3)` `an auxiliary police officer who did not declare office`
#ASSERT NOT `the officer has complied with section 19(3)` `an auxiliary police officer who refused to show the card`
#ASSERT `the refusal to comply is not an offence because the officer did not comply with section 19(3)` `a Commission employee who did not declare office`
#ASSERT NOT `the refusal to comply is not an offence because the officer did not comply with section 19(3)` `a Commission employee appointed by the chief executive who declared office and showed the card`

§§ `20. Power to require documents, articles or information`

-- Document Notice Facts: in writing, to a supplier or person in s 19(1), Commission considers relevant,
-- indicates purpose, accompanied by a copy of ss 27 to 30.
#ASSERT `the Commission may require the production of a document or article or the provision of information` (`Document Notice Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Commission may require the production of a document or article or the provision of information` (`Document Notice Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Commission may require the production of a document or article or the provision of information` (`Document Notice Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Commission may require the production of a document or article or the provision of information` (`Document Notice Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Commission may require the production of a document or article or the provision of information` (`Document Notice Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Commission may require the production of a document or article or the provision of information` (`Document Notice Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the notice complies with section 20(2)` (`Document Notice Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the notice complies with section 20(2)` (`Document Notice Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)

§§ `21. Power to enter premises without warrant`

-- Entry Without Warrant Facts: connected to an investigation, premises reasonably suspected, entrant is an officer or an
-- authorised assistant, written notice given, working days' notice, notice states subject and purpose, notice carries ss 27 to 30,
-- all reasonably practicable steps taken but unable to notify, authorisation evidence produced, information document produced.
`entry on 2 working days' notice` MEANS `Entry Without Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 2, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`entry on 1 working day's notice` MEANS `Entry Without Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 1, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`entry on 5 working days' notice` MEANS `Entry Without Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 5, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`entry on notice that omits the purpose` MEANS `Entry Without Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 3, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`entry on notice with no copy of the offences` MEANS `Entry Without Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 3, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`entry with no notice, and notice could not be given, and documents produced` MEANS `Entry Without Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`entry with no notice, notice could have been given, documents produced` MEANS `Entry Without Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`entry with no notice, notice impracticable, but no authorisation shown` MEANS `Entry Without Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`entry on proper notice to premises not suspected of use` MEANS `Entry Without Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 3, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`entry on proper notice by a stranger` MEANS `Entry Without Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, 3, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the entry without warrant is permitted, with the powers of section 21(5)` `entry on 2 working days' notice`
#ASSERT NOT `the entry without warrant is permitted, with the powers of section 21(5)` `entry on 1 working day's notice`
#ASSERT `the entry without warrant is permitted, with the powers of section 21(5)` `entry on 5 working days' notice`
#ASSERT NOT `the entry without warrant is permitted, with the powers of section 21(5)` `entry on notice that omits the purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `the entry without warrant is permitted, with the powers of section 21(5)` `entry on notice with no copy of the offences`
#ASSERT `the entry without warrant is permitted, with the powers of section 21(5)` `entry with no notice, and notice could not be given, and documents produced`
#ASSERT NOT `the entry without warrant is permitted, with the powers of section 21(5)` `entry with no notice, notice could have been given, documents produced`
#ASSERT NOT `the entry without warrant is permitted, with the powers of section 21(5)` `entry with no notice, notice impracticable, but no authorisation shown`
#ASSERT NOT `the entry without warrant is permitted, with the powers of section 21(5)` `entry on proper notice to premises not suspected of use`
#ASSERT NOT `the entry without warrant is permitted, with the powers of section 21(5)` `entry on proper notice by a stranger`

§§ `22. Power to enter premises under warrant`

`the first condition` MEANS `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on any premises documents which have not been produced as required under section 20 or 21(5)(e)`
`the concealment condition under s 20` MEANS `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on any premises documents which the Commission may require under section 20, and that if required they would be concealed, removed, tampered with or destroyed`
`the concealment condition under s 21` MEANS `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on any premises documents or goods within section 21, and that if notice is given under section 21(2) they would be concealed, removed, tampered with or destroyed`
`the refused entry condition` MEANS `an investigation officer or authorised assistant has attempted to enter under section 21 but been unable to, and there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are documents or goods on the premises`

-- Warrant Facts: applicant is the Commission, conditions, names officer and assistants, states subject and purpose,
-- carries ss 27 to 30, issued on, exercised on, produced to the person, premises unoccupied, steps taken to inform the occupier,
-- occupier informed, opportunity to be present, copy left, premises secured.
`a warrant on the first condition` MEANS `Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the first condition`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 20, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a warrant on the concealment condition under s 20` MEANS `Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the concealment condition under s 20`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 20, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a warrant on the concealment condition under s 21` MEANS `Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the concealment condition under s 21`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 20, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a warrant on the refused entry condition` MEANS `Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the refused entry condition`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 20, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a warrant sought with no condition established` MEANS `Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, EMPTY, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 20, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a warrant sought by someone other than the Commission` MEANS `Warrant Facts` OF FALSE, (LIST `the first condition`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 20, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the court may issue a warrant` `a warrant on the first condition`
#ASSERT `the court may issue a warrant` `a warrant on the concealment condition under s 20`
#ASSERT `the court may issue a warrant` `a warrant on the concealment condition under s 21`
#ASSERT `the court may issue a warrant` `a warrant on the refused entry condition`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may issue a warrant` `a warrant sought with no condition established`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may issue a warrant` `a warrant sought by someone other than the Commission`
-- 22(4): other documents may be authorised only on grounds (b) or (c)
#ASSERT NOT `the court may authorise the power in respect of any other document` `a warrant on the first condition`
#ASSERT `the court may authorise the power in respect of any other document` `a warrant on the concealment condition under s 20`
#ASSERT `the court may authorise the power in respect of any other document` `a warrant on the concealment condition under s 21`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may authorise the power in respect of any other document` `a warrant on the refused entry condition`

-- 22(6): in force for one month beginning on the day it is issued
--                                                  ..., issued on, exercised on, ...
GIVEN issued IS A DATE
      exercised IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Warrant Facts`
`a warrant issued on` issued `and exercised on` exercised MEANS
    `Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the first condition`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, issued, exercised, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the warrant is valid in form and in force when exercised` (`a warrant issued on` (YMD 2026 3 5) `and exercised on` (YMD 2026 3 5))
#ASSERT `the warrant is valid in form and in force when exercised` (`a warrant issued on` (YMD 2026 3 5) `and exercised on` (YMD 2026 4 4))
#ASSERT NOT `the warrant is valid in form and in force when exercised` (`a warrant issued on` (YMD 2026 3 5) `and exercised on` (YMD 2026 4 5))
#ASSERT NOT `the warrant is valid in form and in force when exercised` (`a warrant issued on` (YMD 2026 3 5) `and exercised on` (YMD 2026 3 4))
-- issued 31 Jan: the corresponding date in February is 28 Feb (NOTES.md F5)
#ASSERT `the warrant is valid in form and in force when exercised` (`a warrant issued on` (YMD 2026 1 31) `and exercised on` (YMD 2026 2 27))
#ASSERT NOT `the warrant is valid in form and in force when exercised` (`a warrant issued on` (YMD 2026 1 31) `and exercised on` (YMD 2026 2 28))
-- the form requirements of 22(6)(a) and (b)
#ASSERT NOT `the warrant is valid in form and in force when exercised` (`Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the first condition`), TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 6, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the warrant is valid in form and in force when exercised` (`Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the first condition`), TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 6, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)

-- 22(7) to (10): execution
#ASSERT `the warrant is properly executed` (`a warrant issued on` (YMD 2026 3 5) `and exercised on` (YMD 2026 3 6))
--                                       ..., produced, unoccupied, steps to inform, informed, opportunity, copy left, secured
#ASSERT NOT `the warrant is properly executed` (`Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the first condition`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 6, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the warrant is properly executed` (`Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the first condition`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 6, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the warrant is properly executed` (`Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the first condition`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 6, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `the warrant is properly executed` (`Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the first condition`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 6, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the warrant is properly executed` (`Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the first condition`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 6, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the warrant is properly executed` (`Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the first condition`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 6, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the warrant is properly executed` (`Warrant Facts` OF TRUE, (LIST `the first condition`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 5, YMD 2026 3 6, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)

§§ `23. Post-seizure procedure`

-- Seizure Facts: item is a document, requested a copy, copy provided, owner informed, seized from a vending machine,
-- proprietor or occupier informed, placed in safe custody, proceedings completed, court ordered otherwise, may be evidence.
`a document seized, copy given, owner told, kept safe` MEANS `Seizure Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a document seized, copy asked for but not given` MEANS `Seizure Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`goods seized, no copy asked for` MEANS `Seizure Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`goods seized from a vending machine, proprietor not told` MEANS `Seizure Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`goods seized from a vending machine, proprietor told` MEANS `Seizure Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`seized, owner not told` MEANS `Seizure Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`seized, not kept in safe custody` MEANS `Seizure Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`seized, proceedings still going on` MEANS `Seizure Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`seized, proceedings completed` MEANS `Seizure Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`seized, a court has ordered otherwise` MEANS `Seizure Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`seized, the item cannot be evidence` MEANS `Seizure Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the post-seizure duties have been met` `a document seized, copy given, owner told, kept safe`
#ASSERT NOT `the post-seizure duties have been met` `a document seized, copy asked for but not given`
#ASSERT `the post-seizure duties have been met` `goods seized, no copy asked for`
#ASSERT NOT `the post-seizure duties have been met` `goods seized from a vending machine, proprietor not told`
#ASSERT `the post-seizure duties have been met` `goods seized from a vending machine, proprietor told`
#ASSERT NOT `the post-seizure duties have been met` `seized, owner not told`
#ASSERT NOT `the post-seizure duties have been met` `seized, not kept in safe custody`
#ASSERT `the specified person may retain the goods, document or information` `seized, proceedings still going on`
#ASSERT NOT `the specified person may retain the goods, document or information` `seized, proceedings completed`
#ASSERT NOT `the specified person may retain the goods, document or information` `seized, a court has ordered otherwise`
#ASSERT NOT `the specified person may retain the goods, document or information` `seized, the item cannot be evidence`

§§ `24. and 25. Evidence as to identity; examination and attendance`

-- Examination Facts: reasonably believed to have engaged or abetted, acquainted with the facts, within Singapore,
-- statement in writing, read over, does not understand English, interpreted, signed.
`a person believed to have engaged in an unfair practice` MEANS `Examination Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a witness in Singapore` MEANS `Examination Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a witness abroad` MEANS `Examination Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a person who knows nothing` MEANS `Examination Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the investigation officer may require evidence of identity` `a person believed to have engaged in an unfair practice`
#ASSERT NOT `the investigation officer may require evidence of identity` `a person who knows nothing`
#ASSERT `the investigation officer may examine the person` `a witness in Singapore`
#ASSERT NOT `the investigation officer may examine the person` `a person who knows nothing`
#ASSERT `the person must comply with the written notice to attend` `a witness in Singapore`
#ASSERT NOT `the person must comply with the written notice to attend` `a witness abroad`
#ASSERT NOT `the person must comply with the written notice to attend` `a person who knows nothing`

--                                         in writing, read over, no English, interpreted, signed
#ASSERT `the statement complies with section 25(3)` (`Examination Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the statement complies with section 25(3)` (`Examination Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the statement complies with section 25(3)` (`Examination Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the statement complies with section 25(3)` (`Examination Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the statement complies with section 25(3)` (`Examination Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the statement complies with section 25(3)` (`Examination Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)

§§ `26. Self-incrimination and savings for professional legal advisers`

-- Disclosure Facts: required to disclose, claims incrimination, criminal proceedings, proceedings under Part 3B,
-- professional legal adviser acting in that capacity, privileged communication.
`a required person who claims incrimination, tried for an ordinary crime` MEANS `Disclosure Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a required person who claims incrimination, tried under Part 3B` MEANS `Disclosure Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a required person who made no claim, tried for an ordinary crime` MEANS `Disclosure Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a required person in civil proceedings` MEANS `Disclosure Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a lawyer holding a privileged communication` MEANS `Disclosure Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a lawyer holding a document that is not privileged` MEANS `Disclosure Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a layperson holding a privileged communication` MEANS `Disclosure Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the person is not excused from disclosing on the ground that disclosure might tend to incriminate` `a required person who claims incrimination, tried for an ordinary crime`
#ASSERT `section 26(2) bars admission of the material in the proceedings` `a required person who claims incrimination, tried for an ordinary crime`
#ASSERT NOT `section 26(2) bars admission of the material in the proceedings` `a required person who claims incrimination, tried under Part 3B`
#ASSERT NOT `section 26(2) bars admission of the material in the proceedings` `a required person who made no claim, tried for an ordinary crime`
#ASSERT NOT `section 26(2) bars admission of the material in the proceedings` `a required person in civil proceedings`
#ASSERT `the material is admissible in civil proceedings, including proceedings under the Act` `a required person in civil proceedings`
#ASSERT NOT `the material is admissible in civil proceedings, including proceedings under the Act` `a required person who claims incrimination, tried for an ordinary crime`
#ASSERT `the professional legal adviser is not compelled to disclose the privileged communication` `a lawyer holding a privileged communication`
#ASSERT NOT `the professional legal adviser is not compelled to disclose the privileged communication` `a lawyer holding a document that is not privileged`
#ASSERT NOT `the professional legal adviser is not compelled to disclose the privileged communication` `a layperson holding a privileged communication`
#ASSERT `the adviser must still give the name and address, if known, of the person to whom or by whom the communication was made` `a lawyer holding a privileged communication`
#ASSERT NOT `the adviser must still give the name and address, if known, of the person to whom or by whom the communication was made` `a layperson holding a privileged communication`
